QuestGuidance.Register("en",433,{
[13825]="7004ABA4\n1\tComplete Bhol Rûdh: Trail of Blood\tCandúr can be found in Udûn. You should talk Candúr.\n2\tCompleted\tCompleted Bhol Rûdh: Trail of Blood.\n",
[13826]="700582DE\n1\tSearch for the next location on the map\tThe next mark on the map indicates a location somewhere in Elderslade. You should travel north along the river to search for the next location on the map.\n2\tExamine the old cairn\tThe old cairn can be found in Elderslade. You should examine the cairn.\n3\tTalk to Fróthi\tFróthi can be found following Fram's map in Elderslade. You should talk to Fróthi.\n4\tTalk to Léothred\tLéothred can be found following Fram's map in Elderslade. You should talk to Léothred.\n5\tSearch for the next location on the map\tThe next mark on the map indicates a location somewhere in Elderslade. You should travel north along the river to search for the next location on the map.\n6\tTalk to Léothred\tLéothred can be found following Fram's map in Elderslade. You should talk to Léothred.\n7\tSearch for the next location on the map\tThe next mark on the map indicates a location somewhere in Elderslade. You should travel north along the river to search for the next location on the map.\n8\tExamine the old cairn\tThe old cairn can be found in Elderslade. You should examine the cairn.\n9\tTalk to Léothred\tLéothred can be found following Fram's map in Elderslade. You should talk to Léothred.\n10\tSearch for the next location on the map\tThe next mark on the map lies somewhere in Elderslade. You should travel north along the river to search for the next location on the map.\n11\tTalk to Léothred\tLéothred can be found following Fram's map in Elderslade. You should talk to Léothred.\n12\tSearch for the next location on the map\tThe next mark on the map indicates a location somewhere in Elderslade. You should travel north along the river to search for the next location on the map.\n13\tExamine the old cairn\tThe old cairn can be found in Elderslade. You should examine the cairn.\n14\tTalk to Léothred\tLéothred can be found following Fram's map in Elderslade. You should talk to Léothred.\n15\tSearch for the final location on the map\tThe final mark on the map indicates a location somewhere in Elderslade. You should travel north along the river to search for the next location on the map.\n16\tTalk to Léothred\tLéothred can be found following Fram's map in Elderslade. You should talk to Léothred.\n",
[13827]="700346C1\n1\tDefeat White Hand Warg-trainers (0/6)\tEdsig's Farm appears to have been captured by the White Hand Warg-riders that are ravaging the Fallows' less populated areas.\n2\tDefeat White Hand Warg-trainers (total: 6)\tEdsig's Farm appears to have been captured by the White Hand Warg-riders that are ravaging the Fallows' less populated areas. Some parts of the farm further from the road seem to have been converted for breeding and training of new Wargs for future Warg-riders.\n3\tCompleted\tThe Warg-trainers have been defeated, but more Orcs will come to take their place. Edsig's Farm was not reclaimed from the enemy, but its usefulness to the White Hand has been reduced, for now.\n",
[13828]="700428E3\n1\tTalk to Gaffer Gamgee on Bagshot Row, in Hobbiton\tGaffer Gamgee lives at 3 Bagshot Row, part of the way up the Hill in Hobbiton, north-east of Bingo's hobbit-hole. Bingo has asked you to consult with Gaffer Gamgee and learn if the hobbit learned anything about adventuring from Bilbo Baggins.\n2\tPick up fallen apples in the orchard at Appledores (total: 6)\tThe orchard at Appledores is up the side of the Hill, north-west of Bagshot Row. Gaffer Gamgee has recommended that you pick up some of the fallen apples in the orchard at Appledores to give Bingo a good start on supplies for his journey.\n3\tReturn to Gaffer Gamgee at Bagshot Row\tGaffer Gamgee is waiting for you to return from the Appledores with apples for Bingo.\n4\tBring the apples to Bingo outside his hobbit-hole in Michel Delving\tBingo is outside his hobbit-hole in Michel Delving, just north of the Town Hole. You have a selection of fine apples from the Appledores in Hobbiton to give to Bingo.\n5\tLeave apples by the counter inside the Bird and Baby Inn\tThe Bird and Baby Inn is to the south-west of Bingo's hobbit-hole, in Michel Delving. Bingo cannot stand apples, and has asked you to bring them to the Bird and Baby Inn and leave them by the counter inside. Someone will eat them.\n6\tTalk to Esmerelda Burrows in the Bird and Baby Inn\tEsmerelda Burrows has gotten your attention inside the Bird and Baby Inn, and wishes to speak with you about something.\n7\tTalk to Bingo outside his hobbit-hole in Michel Delving\tBingo is at his home north-east of the Bird and Baby Inn. You have left the basket of apples in the Bird and Baby Inn, but in the process Esmerelda Burrows managed to discover that Bingo is planning a journey.\n8\tTalk to Bingo by the Stocktower, south of the town of Stock\tBingo asked you to meet him at the Stocktower south of the town of Stock. He plans to climb the tower in order to build up the physical prowess he will need for his journey.\n9\tTalk to Bingo in the Golden Perch Inn, in the town of Stock\tBingo tried to climb the Stocktower, and has given up. He says he will meet you in the Golden Perch Inn, in the town of Stock, to continue his training.\n",
[13829]="70053F1E\n1\tSpar with Faratúr\tFaratúr can be found in Díngarth. You should spar with Faratúr.\n2\tSpar with Armacar\tArmacar can be found in Díngarth. You should spar with Armacar.\n3\tSpar with Estenan\tEstenan can be found in Díngarth. You should spar with Estenan.\n4\tSpar with Tulcandur\tTulcandur can be found in Díngarth. You should spar with Tulcandur.\n5\tSpar with Celuher\tCeluher can be found in Díngarth. You should spar with Celuher.\n6\tSpar with Hallatan\tHallatan can be found in Díngarth. You should spar with Hallatan.\n7\tSpar with Ambassion\tAmbassion can be found in Díngarth. You should spar with Ambassion.\n8\tSpar with Ostondil\tOstondil can be found in Díngarth. You should spar with Ostondil.\n9\tTalk to Hildvar\tHildvar can be found in Díngarth. You should talk to Hildvar.\n",
[13830]="70062234\n1\tUse your Battle Shout on the training dummy, then strike it with your skill Devastating Blow\tUse Devastating Blowon the training dummy nearby. HINT: Captains rely on their Battle Shout to put them into a Battle-Readied State. While in this state, Captains can use special skills such as Devastating Blow, an effective attack that deals a great deal of damage. Attack the Training Dummy with your Battle Shout to put you into a Battle-Readied State and then attack the dummy with your Devastating Blow.\n2\tTalk to the Captain Trainer at the Edhelion Watch\tThe Captain Trainer is at the Edhelion Watch. Now that you have successfully used your Devastating Blow, you should return to your trainer and tell them of your success.\n",
[13831]="700244B2\n1\tStrike the Training-dummy with 'Shield-swipe'\tUse your Shield-swipe skill on the Training-dummy nearby. HINT: Guardians rely on Reactive Skills to deal damage and generate Threat against their enemies. Shield-swipe requires that the Guardian Block an incoming enemy attack before they can use the skill. Head over to the Training-dummies to the north of the trainer and attack it until you successfully block one of their attacks. If you're having trouble getting a block, try using Guardian's Ward to increase your chances of blocking enemy attacks. Once you have blocked an attack you will be able to use your Shield-swipe skill. Strike the Training-dummy with Shield-swipe.\n2\tTalk to the Guardian Trainer at the Edhelion Watch\tThe Guardian Trainer is at the Edhelion Watch. Now that you have successfully used your newly-learned skill, you should return to your trainer and tell her of your success.\n",
[13832]="70019509\n1\tStrike the Training-dummy with Penetrating Shot\tUse Penetrating Shot on the Training-dummy nearby. HINT: Hunters need Focus to use some of their special shots, and Penetrating Shot is such a skill. Use your Quick Shot ability until you have three Focus points, then use Penetrating Shot.\n2\tTalk to the Hunter Trainer in Archet\tThe Hunter Trainer is in Archet, near the south gate. Now that you have successfully used your skill, you should return to your trainer and tell him of your success.\n",
[13833]="700244B3\n1\tUse Penetrating Shot against a Training Dummy\tUse Penetrating Shot on the training-dummy nearby. HINT: Hunters need Focus to use some of their special shots, and Penetrating Shot is such a skill. Use your Quick Shot ability until you have three Focus points, then use Penetrating Shot.\n2\tTalk to the Hunter Trainer at the Edhelion Watch\tThe Hunter Trainer is at the Edhelion Watch. Now that you have successfully used your skill, you should return to your trainer and tell her of your success.\n",
[13834]="700244B6\n1\tStrike the training-dummy with Burning Embers\tUse the skill Burning Embers on the training-dummy nearby.\n2\tTalk to the Lore-master Trainer at the Edhelion Watch\tThe Lore-master Trainer is at the Edhelion Watch. Now that you have successfully used your newly-learned skill, you should return to your trainer and tell her of your success.\n",
[13835]="700244B5\n1\tLearn the skill 'Major Ballad' and use it while in combat with a Training Dummy\tHINT: Minstrels use Ballads to attack their enemies, lightly heal their fellows and empower themselves. These skills operate on a rotating system that allows the minstrel to have three special buffs on themselves at any time. After the third buff is applied the next Ballad played will overwrite the first, then the second and so on.\n2\tTalk to the Minstrel Trainer at the Edhelion Watch\tThe Minstrel Trainer is at the Edhelion Watch. Now that you have successfully used your skill, you should return to your trainer and tell him of your success.\n",
[13836]="700244B4\n1\tUse your skill 'Fiery Ridicule' on the Training Dummy nearby\tUse your skill Fiery Ridicule on the Training Dummy nearby. HINT: Rune-keepers require Battle Attunement to use offensive skills, and Healing Attunement to cast healing spells. Attunement is raised or lowered through the use of similar skills. Offensive Skills typically have red backgrounds, and Healing skills typically have green backgrounds.\n2\tTalk to the Rune-keeper Trainer at the Edhelion Watch\tThe Rune-keeper Trainer is at the Edhelion Watch. Now that you have successfully used your skill, you should return to your trainer and tell her of your success.\n",
[13837]="70062235\n1\tStrike the training-dummy with Fiery Ridicule\tUse your skill Fiery Ridicule on the training-dummy. HINT: Rune-keepers require Battle Attunement to use offensive skills, and Healing Attunement to cast healing spells. Attunement is raised or lowered through the use of similar skills. Offensive Skills typically have red backgrounds, and Healing skills typically have green backgrounds.\n2\tTalk to the Rune-keeper Trainer in Archet\tThe Rune-keeper Trainer is in Archet. Now that you have successfully used Fiery Ridicule, you should return to your trainer and tell them of your success.\n",
[13838]="700244B7\n1\tUse Deft Strike against a Training Dummy\tUse deft strike on the training-dummy nearby. HINT: Wardens use combinations of their basic skills such as Quick Thrust and Shield-Bash to build more powerful Gambit attacks. To use your Deft Strike skill, attack a Training-Dummy with your Quick Thrust ability twice. This should cause your Gambit Default skill to change into your Deft Strike skill. Use your Deft Strike ability to strike a Training-Dummy.\n2\tTalk to the Warden Trainer at the Edhelion Watch\tThe Warden Trainer is at the Edhelion Watch. Now that you have successfully used your Deft Strike, you should return to your trainer and tell him of your success.\n",
[13839]="70062233\n1\tStrike the training dummy with Surprise Strike\tUse your Surprise Strike skill against the nearby training dummy. HINT: Burglars benefit greatly from Critical Strikes and Devastating Blows. Scoring such hits will allow them to use special skills such as Double-edged Strike. In addition, many Burglar skills benefit from being in Stealth. Try attacking a training dummy from Stealth with Surprise Strike to inflict even more damage.\n2\tTalk to the Burglar Trainer at the Edhelion Watch\tThe Burglar Trainer is at the Edhelion Watch. Now that you have successfully used your Surprise Strike, you should return to your trainer and tell them of your success.\n",
[13840]="700244B1\n1\tLearn the skill 'Savage Strikes' and use it against a Training Dummy\tUse your new skill Savage Strikes on the training-dummy nearby. HINT: Champions rely on Fervour to activate some of their skills such as Savage Strikes. Use your Swift Strike skill to build 2 Fervour and then strike the Targeting Dummy with your Savage Strikes skill.\n2\tTalk to the Champion Trainer at the Edhelion Watch\tThe Champion Trainer is at the Edhelion Watch. Now that you have successfully used your newly-learned skill, return to your trainer and tell him of your success.\n",
[13841]="700586C7\n1\tUse your Overhand Smash skill on the Training Dummy (total: 3)\tUse your new skill Overhand Smash on the training dummy nearby. Brawlers rely on Mettle to activate some of their skills such as Overhand Smash. Use your Low Strike or Dextrous Hook to build 3 Mettle and then strike the Training Dummy with your Overhand Smash skill.\n2\tTalk to Naithador, the Brawler Trainer at the Edhelion Watch\tNaithador, the Brawler Trainer, is at the Edhelion Watch. Now that you have successfully used your newly-learned skill, return to your trainer and tell him of your success.\n",
[13842]="700173CB\n1\tDefeat Ilzkâl\030Defeat Nardur\tIlzkâl and Nardur can be found in the Grand Stair, north-east of the Orc-watch. Thithrand believes that the Uruk-hai Nardur and Ilzkâl may be planning to revolt against Igash and steal the tribute kept within his throne for themselves.\n2\tTalk to Thithrand at the Orc-watch\tThithrand is at the Orc-watch, south-west of the Grand Stair. You should return to Thithrand with news of your victory.\n",
[13843]="70053152\n1\tTraitorous Woodmen can be found in the warrens of Tûn Melen. Tautila has asked you to find and, if necessary, defeat his traitorous kinsfolk who have joined Sharkey's Men.\t\n2\tTalk to Tautila in the warrens of Tûn Melen\tTautila can be found in the warrens of Tûn Melen. You have found or defeated all of the traitorous Woodmen in service to Sharkey. You should return to Tautila.\n",
[13844]="70002E17\n1\tSearch for evidence of the dwarves' location\tA boar herd can be found in the South Trollshaws, at a place called Lavanim, west of Barachen's camp. Barachen asked you to search for the missing dwarves among the boars of the South Trollshaws.\n2\tSearch for evidence of the dwarf-company upon the boars of Lavanim\tA boar herd can be found in the South Trollshaws, at a place called Lavanim, west of Barachen's camp. Barachen asked you to search for the missing dwarves among the boars to the west of his camp. Perhaps you may find more evidence upon the boars of Lavanim.\n3\tBring the scrap of cloth you found to Barachen\tBarachen is at his camp in the South Trollshaws, south of the road and in the shadow of tall cliffs. Barachen is waiting to hear whether you found any sign of the missing dwarves among the boars of the Trollshaws.\n",
[13845]="70027B5B\n1\tBreak snap-jaw traps (total: 5)\tSnap-jaw traps have been placed in the undergrowth on the western shore of the lake in Tâl Methedras. Déormund has given you a heavy stone with which to smash the snap-jaw traps you find.\n2\tReturn the heavy stone to Déormund\tDéormund is waiting to speak with you on the western shore of the lake in Tâl Methedras.\n",
[13846]="70030A9C\n1\tHuorns are trapped throughout the Silkenhold in northern Fangorn, ensnared by cruel and sticky webs. You should free the Huorns from their bonds.\t\n2\tTalk to the Huorn at the entrance\tThe Huorn who sent you on this perilous mission is at the foot of the stair leading to the Silkenhold. You should speak with the Huorn and tell him that his friends are now safe from the spiders' traps.\n",
[13847]="7005A2EA\n1\tCollect trapped fish (total: 6)\030Collect trapped critters (total: 6)\tFish traps can be found around the shores of the nearby river. Traps for critters are scattered throughout the forests outside the eastern gate of Amdân. You should check the traps for fish and critters.\n2\tTalk to Elgur\tElgur is in Amdân. You should bring the fish and critters to Elgur.\n",
[13848]="7006AB2E\n1\tFreed spider victims (total: 8)\tThe spiders north of Mekab-kuphâr in Nishabêt have seized a party of Temámir Dwarves. Rescue them before they are devoured!\n2\tReturn to Temámir Guard Captain Nûru\tReturn to Temámir Guard Captain Nûru in the Temámir outpost in southern Khabârkhad.\n",
[13849]="7004A907\n1\tCollect the crate of traps\tLegolas has hidden the crate of traps in the Rath Cail. You should collect the crate of traps.\n2\tPlace Orkish traps (total: 5)\030Defeat Mordor Tracker (total: 5)\tIdeal trap locations can be found in the Rath Cail. You should place traps in these locations, and then defeat the Mordor Trackers that stumble into them.\n",
[13850]="7006AAB4\n1\tTalk to Temámir Guard Captain Nûru in Mekab-kuphâr\tKhôltekh has asked that you deploy traps along the northern walls of Khabârkhad in the Umbar-môkh. He has directed you to speak with Nûru, who can be found in Mekab-kuphâr, a guard outpost in southern Khabârkhad.\n2\tTalk to the vendor Mâramit in Tilmakhím\tNûru told you to go far to the north, outside Khabârkhad, to Tilmakhím in Tâkhdar. There, a vendor named Mâramit will give you the traps Khôltekh asked you to place.\n3\tDeploy traps near Lôkhalel on the northern edge of Khabârkhad (total: 8)\tGo south of Tilmakhím, to the northern edge of Khabârkhad, near Lôkhalel, and deploy the traps Mâramit gave you.\n4\tReturn to Khôltekh in the Hall of the Kindred\tReturn to Khôltekh in Dâr Laja, the Hall of the Kindred.\n",
[13851]="70059438\n1\tPlace traps in the Wildwood (quantity: see journal)\tGood trap locations can be found in the Wildwood. You should place the traps you have been given in the Wildwood.\n2\tTalk to Grun Curldock\tGrun Curldock can be found at Trader's Wharf. You should talk to Grun Curldock.\n",
[13852]="7001F296\n1\tTalk to Danfennas at Helethir\tDanfennas is at Helethir, north-east of Mithechad. Perindúr has asked you to speak with his friend Danfennas regarding the plague upon the trees of the Ashenslades.\n",
[13853]="70046C47\n1\tListen to Anborn's tale\tAnborn can be found at Henneth Annûn in North Ithilien. Anborn has offered to tell you a tale of strange travellers that passed through Ithilien.\n2\tTalk to Anborn at Henneth Annûn\tAnborn can be found at Henneth Annûn in North Ithilien. You have listened to Anborn's tale and should now ask if he knows more of these travellers.\n",
[13854]="7004F91C\n1\tFind Ingór, son of Vékun in the Keep of Tharrazhâr\tIngór, son of Vékun can be found in the Keep of Tharrazhâr. Dori has asked you to speak to Ingór, son of Vékun before following the Men Angrún to Óinsbridge.\n2\tTalk to Ingór, son of Vékun\tIngór, son of Vékun can be found in the Keep of Tharrazhâr. Dori has asked you to speak to Ingór, son of Vékun before following the Men Angrún to Óinsbridge.\n3\tFollow the roadway to Óinsbridge and rejoin Dori and Company\tÓinsbridge can be found far to the south-west of Skarháld. You have spoken to Ingór, son of Vékun, and you should now follow the Men Angrún to Óinsbridge.\n4\tTalk to Dori at Óinsbridge\tDori can be found at Óinsbridge. You have arrived at Óinsbridge and should now speak to Dori.\n5\tSearch Óinsbridge for signs of Nori's expedition\tSigns of Nori's expedition might be found at Óinsbridge. Dori has asked you to search Óinsbridge for signs of Nori's expedition.\n6\tThe abandoned camp-site can be found in Óinsbridge. You have found an abandoned camp-site in Óinsbridge. You should try to determine if this camp-site was built by Nori and his expedition.\t\n7\tFollow the path of hoof-prints leading away from the abandoned camp-site\tA path of hoof-prints can be found in Óinsbridge. You have discovered a path of hoof-prints leading away from the abandoned camp-site. You should follow them.\n8\tTalk to Bofur at Óinsbridge\tBofur can be found at Óinsbridge. The path of hoof-prints has led you to Bofur and his goat. You should talk to Bofur.\n9\tFollow the path of hoof-prints leading away from Óinsbridge\tA path of hoof-prints can be found on the Men Angrún to the west of Óinsbridge. Bofur has discovered another trail of hoof-prints leading onto the Men Angrún to the west of Óinsbridge. You should follow them.\n10\tDirect the raven to fly to Dori at Óinsbridge\tThe raven can be found atop an obelisk along the Men Angrún to the west of Óinsbridge. The path of hoof-prints led down the Men Angrún, but it appears that one of Arcah's ravens has perched atop an old obelisk along the dark road. You should direct the raven to fly to Dori at Óinsbridge.\n11\tTalk to Dori at Óinsbridge\tDori can be found at Óinsbridge. You have directed the raven to fly to Dori at Óinsbridge. You should now return to Dori.\n",
[13855]="70032920\n1\tDefeat vicious Wold Wargs in the south plains (total: 8)\tWargs prowl the southern fields of the Wold near the border of the Norcrofts, south of the small trader outpost on the road. You should defeat the vicious Wold Wargs so that the travellers will be safe from harm.\n2\tReturn to the merchants' outpost\tThe frightened merchant can be found on the southern part of the road leading towards the Norcrofts, at a small trading outpost. You should reassure the frightened man that the threat is lessened, and the Wargs will trouble his vulnerable outpost no more.\n",
[13856]="70047A57\n1\tAdd black powder mix to Orc fire-pits (total: 8)\tOrc fire-pits can be found around the Slag-hills. You should add the black powder mix to Orc fire-pits to produce a smoky haze.\n2\tCompleted\tThe black powder smoke now obstructs the view from the Towers of the Teeth.\n",
})
